"""Render the completed evidence, keep only sampled finalists and rebuild inputs."""
from core import *
import statistics,collections
from batch import report
def main():
 report();rows=[json.loads(l)for f in OUT.glob('*results.jsonl')for l in f.read_text().splitlines()]
 mc=json.loads((OUT/'mc_results.json').read_text());sampled=[]
 for name,seeds in mc.items():
  if len(seeds)==3:sampled.append((sum(x['score']for x in seeds.values())/3,name,seeds))
 sampled.sort();best=next(x for x in sampled if x[2]['0']['acceptance']>=.5)
 mean,name,seeds=best;bm=next(x[0]for x in sampled if x[1]=='base')
 bestmeta=json.loads((OUT/name).with_suffix('.json').read_text());bestrow=next(r for r in rows if r['stem']==name)
 (OUT/'best.qasm').write_bytes((OUT/name).with_suffix('.qasm').read_bytes());(OUT/'best.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(bestmeta,source_finalist=name,mc_mean=mean,mc_seeds=seeds),indent=2)+'\n')
 text=(OUT/'REPORT.md').read_text();text=text.replace('Status: running — full-circuit structural screens; MC finalists pending.',f'Status: structural screen complete — {len(rows)} full-circuit recipes evaluated; delivery MC verified; slow A-state-reuse MC remains unverified; no submission made.')
 header=['',f'Delivery: [best.qasm](best.qasm) and [best.json](best.json), identical to `{name}`. Three-seed mean **{mean:.9e}**, versus the control **{bm:.9e}** ({100*(mean/bm-1):+.3f}%). Seed-0 acceptance **{seeds["0"]["acceptance"]:.8f}**. Exact total **{bestrow["total"]:.9e}**, {bestrow["CX"]} CX, native R={bestrow["R"]}.',
 'The observed MC means select this delivery; the exact and three-seed rankings agree for the blue-XZ finalist, the prior 21-CX blue-X finalist, and the base. No global optimum is claimed. The 25-CX injection control and the 19-CX blue-X check have a near-tie that changes order between the two estimators; that diagnostic tie remains unresolved because 100 re-draws were not performed. It does not determine this delivery.','',
 '| Sampled circuit | Exact total | MC seed 0 | MC 1000 | MC 2000 | Three-seed mean | Acceptance seed 0 |',
 '|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
 for avg,n,ss in sampled:
  rr=next(r for r in rows if r['stem']==n)
  header.append('| %s | %.9e | %.9e | %.9e | %.9e | %.9e | %.8f |'%(n,rr['total'],ss['0']['score'],ss['1000']['score'],ss['2000']['score'],avg,ss['0']['acceptance']))
 text=text.replace('\nBar:', '\n'+'\n'.join(header)+'\n\nBar:',1)
 text=text.replace('; MC unverified.','; this is a mathematical screen, not a completed MC rank.')
 d=json.loads((OUT/'decomposition.json').read_text());abl=json.loads((OUT/'ablation.json').read_text());no={r['region']:r for r in abl if r['mode']=='no'}
 components=['injection','stabilizer','T_layers','check1','check2','internal_idle']
 lines=['','## Mechanisms and evidence','',
 '- **Internal exposure dominates the pre-stage opportunity.** Making the pre-stage noiseless lowers total loss from 7.13059568e-5 to 5.12292461e-5 (−28.15%); its net cubic term drops from 1.69860290e-5 to 3.68176464e-6 (−78.32%). Removing only internal pre-stage idles gives 5.41148770e-5 (−24.11%). Pre-stage-only loss is 3.93363873e-6; the remaining 1.61430720e-5 of its full-vs-no-pre effect is cross-region interaction, including normalization. [Ablation](ablation.json).',
 '- **Logical Z triples through long data waits.** The largest explicit triple is Z on q10 at steps 31–44, q3 at 28–43, and q0 at 30–43, contributing 1.13019773e-7. These are code positions {3,4,0}, a weight-three logical-Z support. q10 is a hop-owned idle; q0/q3 are pre-owned. Raw triples containing an internal pre idle sum to 1.25480688e-5 (59.1% of raw weight-three mass). The raw 2.12287688e-5 triple sum and −4.24273979e-6 pair-times-others term must be combined to obtain the cubic term. [Complete grouped sets](decomposition.json).',
 '- **A faults combine with old data errors.** A×pre pairs contribute 4.12194362e-6; 3.13083992e-6 of that pairs A with internal pre idles. A×hop adds 2.75187758e-6. Several top pairs combine a q10 Z idle with ZZ/ZI/XY/IZ errors in the final A-encoder CXs; each displayed aggregated-channel pair contributes 3.08429142e-7. This supports the mechanism of correlated A Z errors completing a logical support with one surviving data error. Pair attribution is measured; this propagation description is an inference from the exact fault signatures.',
 '- **The encoder alone has little intrinsic second-order opportunity.** No harmful pair in the base decomposition involves an injection-encoder channel; making those channels noiseless changes only the cubic term, lowering total by 5.59471688e-7. Substituting 21 CX instead of 19 helps the check combination by advancing its schedule, while the 21-CX encoder alone does not beat the base on the measured MC mean.',
 '- **The new check must retain its fault detection.** A blue X stabilizer check with the Bell uncompute passes and helps. Omitting the unbell CX, then taking parity of both ancilla readouts, changes the blue-X exact loss from 7.03407384e-5 to 9.56469790e-5, mainly through the second-order term (5.35873985e-5 to 7.82738108e-5). The saved CX costs more in undetected pairs than it saves in noise. [Unbell-free receipt](cat_1_x_0_0.exact.json).',
 '- **Acceptance trades are real circuit changes.** Full H_XY repetition (24 added CX) and full stabilizer rounds extend R to 55–58 and fail acceptance. Smaller blue X/XZ checks were rebuilt with each encoder, reversed Bell orientation, cat/A state reuse, and selected optional suffix checks removed. Every trade is separately scored in the table; acceptance is not an objective.',
 '- **Compression is not equivalent to removing idle noise.** Minimum pre-gap schedules recover acceptance but move exposure into later data/block lifetimes. The fixed-suffix compact control is 7.58885274e-5 despite higher acceptance 0.55563; the ablation ceiling cannot be claimed as an implementable gain.',
 '- **Corrected failure mechanisms.** A late q13 flag initially overwrote an active BC state; the reserved-lifetime variant delays BC and was re-evaluated. Bare-cat individual MX results are random even when their parity is fixed; q10 must be reset after the last native measurement before its |+>-based data hop. The corrected postreset recipes pass noiseless correctness but lose on fidelity/acceptance. A Z-measurement replacing a reused injection reset is not a deterministic preparation and fails correctness. These failures do not exclude other flags or measurement-based designs.','',
 '| Component | Pair attribution (split half per fault) | Raw triple attribution (split thirds) | Total with this component noiseless |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
 for comp in components:
  p=sum(v*k.split(' x ').count(comp)/2 for k,v in d['pairs_component'].items());t=sum(v*k.split(' x ').count(comp)/3 for k,v in d['triples_component'].items())
  lines.append('| %s | %.9e | %.9e | %.9e |'%(comp,p,t,no[comp]['total']))
 lines+=['','## Coverage and limits','',
 '- Tested: full H_XY repetition at two boundaries; full X-first/Z-first colour-code rounds at two boundaries; single/two-colour X, Z, and XZ checks; pre-stage RX verification and measurement-init; three borrowed cat-flag locations; full/rigid suffix compaction; 19/21/24/25-CX injections; all 16 protected parity-network forms plus compact acceptance trades; all six D4 embedding classes plus code-automorphism search; unbell-free cats and the corrected q10 reuse; coupled check/encoder/acceptance trades. Different schedules with identical SHA-256 are retained as separate recipe rows, not independent evidence.',
 '- Embeddings use FREELAY’s legal 48 placements modulo D4 (six representatives), current prefix per-wire dependencies, joint82 B/C and the L5 A template. The search is bounded to three data hops per wire. It is not an exhaustive search over arbitrary cultivation graphs, dynamic encoder topology, or all code relabellings. The automorphism solver returned FEASIBLE, not an optimality certificate.',
 '- All 16 alternative forms are physically rebuilt with the current suffix and independently checked; their parity networks still fail acceptance after the tested compaction trades. This closes those networks only. Full reference exact2 receipts verify the sampled check finalists; other late screens use the same exact2 model with BCSYN2’s validated Fourier-moment contraction. The base decomposition independently reproduces the unmodified evaluator total to numerical precision.',
 '- Verified: judge checks, native schedules, adjacency, hashes, exact c1/second/third coefficients, the full loss partition, and the listed 1e8-shot MC samples. Inferred: general mechanisms beyond the explicit fault sets and which untested redesign might win. Unverified: a global optimum and sub-percent true-mean ordering without many re-draws. No external submission result is claimed.',
 '- **Uncompleted slow-MC branch:** A q1 state reuse gives 6.93155844e-5 exact for the low-c2 XZ trade; q2 reuse with both optional A checks removed gives 6.92743643e-5. Noisy sampling of 100,000 shots takes 12.71–13.22 s on owl versus 0.42–0.44 s for the corresponding reset circuits; setup is under 0.5 s. Sixteen noise-equivalent instruction reorderings of each of two q1-reuse circuits did not repair this. Linear projection is approximately 3.5–3.7 h for the serial 1e8-shot judge, beyond its one-hour cap on this host. That projection is an inference, not an official timeout. The already-running 20-worker MC attempt on the related q1-reuse X-check candidate was terminated by its exact Docker container ID; its 1e8 score and the slow branch’s final MC rank remain unverified. [q1 timing](profile_mc.log), [q2 timing](profile_q2.log), [order trials](sampler_order.log). The winning non-reuse circuit completed all three required 1e8-shot runs.',
 '- Four cat measure-init build attempts failed the native-fold audit and were not scored: cat_1_x_1_0, cat_1_x_1_1, cat_1_z_1_0, cat_1_z_1_1. Their proposed M in place of a reset changes how the preceding MX is folded, so they cannot be treated as the intended one-step replacement. [Build log](refine.log). All emitted circuits, including failed judge recipes, have rows in the main table.',
 '- The task-scoped file/host restrictions were followed. Computation used owl only through Docker and small local construction/audit processes with numerical threads fixed to one. No credentials, submissions, commits, pushes, other-lane writes, or sub-agents were used.',
 '- Primary sources read: [judge noise](../../../upstream/snu-qff2026-problem/tprep/noise.py), [exact2](../EVAL/exact2.py), [Gidney cultivation construction](../../../upstream/magic-state-cultivation/src/cultiv/_construction/_cultivation_stage.py), [TREP](../TREP/REPORT.md), [TREP2](../TREP2/REPORT.md), [FREELAY](../FREELAY/REPORT.md). Claims here are from those local sources and the linked measurements, not memory.','']
 text+='\n'.join(lines);(OUT/'REPORT.md').write_text(text)
 (OUT/'delivery.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(stem=name,mc_mean=mean,base_mean=bm,relative_change=mean/bm-1,exact=bestrow,mc=seeds),indent=2)+'\n')
 print(name,mean,flush=True)
if __name__=='__main__':main()
